WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.000
[Gospel chorus singing.]

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.580
[Narrator:] I want you to meet Mrs. Mary Cooley, a midwife, who lives in Albany, Georgia.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.200
[Mary is shown ironing.]

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.930
[Narrator:] This is a story of how she helps people,

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:30.890
people like Ida Fleming who engaged Miss Mary to deliver her third child.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:39.530
People like Adam and Marybell Dudley, newcomers to Dougherty County who bring their troubles to this midwife. 

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.980
In the county health department are doctors and nurses who help Miss Mary

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:51.430
do the job to which she and thousands of other midwives all over the south

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:56.550
have dedicated their lives: of birthing of healthy babies.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:04.880
[Chorus singing.]

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:08.210
[Ida looks at wall filled with photos of infants and children.]

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:10.910
[Ida:] All these your babies, Miss Mary?

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:13.810
[Miss Mary:] Yes. They is all my babies. 

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:18.290
Delivered about 1,400. [Inaudible] come this year.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:24.770
[Ida:] Here's my two. I'm gonna send you a real little baby picture of this next one, Miss Mary.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:27.100
[Miss Mary:] Well, you do that then, honey.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.550
[Mary is packing her medical bag.]

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:31.800
[Chorus singing.]

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:40.380
[Miss Mary:] Lord, that Ida. Ain't nothing bothering her now, but I remember four years ago she was so scared. 

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.940
I had to take her to the clinic myself.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:48.170
Back in those days, our clinic was meeting at the old building.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:51.760
[A white man and a white woman are at the front of the room, addressing several African-American midwives.]

00:02:51.760 --> 00:03:01.020
[Miss Mary:] Dr. Andrew had been our health officer, for I guess just about a year.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.680
[Miss Dixon:] Ida Fleming?

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:13.740
[Chorus singing.]

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:25.940
[Ida follows the nurse into an exam room.]

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:31.500
[Miss Mary:] Little Miss Dixon always try to help mommas feel easy the first time in the clinic.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.270
Of course, I foretold Ida already what they going to do.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.950
[Miss Dixon takes Ida's vital signs, smiling and speaking to Ida.]

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:47.370
[Miss Mary:] How they take each mother's temperature and feel their pulse.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:53.590
Every time a mother comes to the clinic, they measure her blood pressure.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:59.570
That's another way they can tell if she's keeping in good shape or, if she ain't,

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:13.300
the things she had better do to get herself well so she can have her baby more easy and normal.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.770
[Laughter] 

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:17.760
[Miss Mary:] Ida's doing just fine.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:24.530
The first visit they draw off a little blood for a test and in eight months they do the same. 

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:31.770
That's to see if the mother need to take the treatments.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:39.460
Every time the mother comes to the clinic she brings along a little bottle of her water for a urine test.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.730
That's to make sure that her kidneys is working all right. 

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:47.360
When our patients begin their check-up early like Ida did,

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:55.440
then we midwives ain't so have to run up against something beyond our handling.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.770
Dr. Newton examines all the mothers the first time they come into the clinic

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:04.050
and again in eight months and between times if they need it.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.620
[Ida sits at the edge of the examining table and the doctor walks over to her.]

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:22.040
[Miss Mary:] When it come Ida's time for the doctor, she knowed already it wasn't nothing for her to be scared about.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:26.440
[Ida and Miss Mary laughing] 

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:29.120
[Ida:] I didn't know nothing when I first come to see you.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:32.660
[Miss Mary:] Yes, honey, but you knows a-plenty now.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:36.150
Come on over and let's look at your baby things.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:41.000
[Chorus singing.]

00:05:41.000 --> 00:06:05.360
[Mary and Ida walk over to Ida's home.]

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:11.990
[Miss Mary:] I always visit my mommas ahead of time if I possibly can get to it. 

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:17.680
'course I knowed before I got here Aunt Mattie and Ida would have everything fixed up nice.

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:23.110
[Chorus singing.]

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:35.580
[Midwives, pregnant women, and their families are shown preparing for deliveries: 

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:55.530
sterilizing items, folding and arranging bedding and cloths, and tending to older children.]

00:06:55.530 --> 00:07:05.560
[Chorus singing.]

00:07:05.560 --> 00:08:03.090
[Preparations continue for the birth of a new baby.]

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:09.380
[Midwives are seated in rows in a meeting room, talking amongst themselves.]

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.100
[A doctor is seated at the front of the room.]

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.370
[Midwife:] Mary late this morning.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:17.670
[Midwives:] Yeah!

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:27.020
[Doctor:] Two days ago a baby delivered by a midwife died when it ought to have lived.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:32.890
As your health officer, it was my duty to find out why that baby died. 

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:39.590
My examination showed that its cord got infected and you all know what that means. 

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:42.920
Something wasn't clean. 

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:47.210
Maybe the midwife didn't boil her scissors long enough,

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:53.660
or it could have been that the dressing she used wasn't sterile,

00:08:53.660 --> 00:09:03.220
or it might have been that she got in a hurry and didn't wash her hands well. 

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:07.420
You midwives in this county have built up a wonderful reputation. 

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:13.880
You work hard and I know how difficult it is to keep things clean in some of the homes where you have to go.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.270
[Midwife:] That's right.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:22.380
[Doctor:] But your record shows that you can keep clean and when something like this happens, it's a warning to all of us.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:33.780
To us doctors, the nurses as well as to you midwives. It shows us how very easily we can slip back when we get careless.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:43.850
[Midwives are seated around a table with a doll figure lying on it, practicing tying off the umbilical cord.]

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.770
[Miss Mary:] I've been doing the same thing about 18 years,

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:53.730
but I still know I can slip if I don't keep checking on myself. 

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:56.130
These young girls who are just starting out, 

00:09:56.130 --> 00:10:02.080
they have an advantage because they are learning the right way at the beginning,

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:10.010
but you know old folks can change too if they just put their mind to it.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:25.690
[Adam and Maybell arrive at Miss Mary's home to speak with her about delivering their baby.]

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:29.410
[Miss Mary:] You people seem to be new around here to me.

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:31.800
[Adam:] Yes'm.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:37.550
[Miss Mary:] Well, how far are you along with this pregnancy, honey?

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:42.460
[Maybell:] About six or seven months, I think.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:45.690
[Miss Mary:] What did the doctor say about your case, honey?

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:48.860
[Adam:] She ain't seen no doctor.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:55.370
[Miss Mary:] Oh well, before I can take her case she'll have to see a doctor.

00:10:55.370 --> 00:11:00.700
She'll have to take a blood test and go through an examination.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.300
[Adam:] What's all that for?

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:07.320
[Miss Mary:] It's for the protection of her and also her baby. 

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:10.470
How you know but what she don't need treatment? 

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:13.860
Maybell, is this your first baby?

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:17.680
[Maybell:] No, it ain't.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:23.930
[Miss Mary:] Well, just tell me, honey, how did you get along with all your pregnancies?

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:32.940
[Adam:] Our first one come dead. The next one dropped before she got far along with it.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:40.160
[Miss Mary:] Well, you just got to see a doctor. 

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:42.430
Maybell, I tell you what to do.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.540
Come on down to the clinic Friday morning, hear?

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.220
[Adam:] That's not going to hurt you.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:51.660
[Miss Mary:] 'Course not. It's not going to hurt you. 

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:54.560
Y'all stop by at four now and I'll go with you.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.330
[Adam:] Thank you, Miss Mary. I'll bring her by.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:12:02.150
[Miss Mary:] All right.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:07.040
Dr. Newton said Maybell ain't been eating right and it shows up on her.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:11.130
[Maybell is lying on an exam table. Dr. Newton touches discolorations on her face.]

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:19.020
[Miss Mary:] He says every mother oughta have a good examination all over as soon as she thinks she's pregnant. 

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:25.930
He said Maybell ought to have start getting her check-up months ago. 

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:36.430
Poor Miss Penny, sure got a problem on her hands.

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:40.370
Yes, that was just my day for trouble.

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:48.050
Another lady there just begging to be my patient, but I most know she needed the doctor.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:55.510
[The doctor, Miss Mary, and another woman sit together at a table in the clinic.]

00:12:55.510 --> 00:13:03.460
[Miss Mary:] Dr. Newton said I was right about that thing and he showed me a danger sign.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:07.810
The lady has been having sharp headaches all the time. 

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:16.140
The doctor said being pregnant right by itself is no cause for a healthy woman to feel all dizzy and drug out.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:19.470
[The doctor palpates the pregnant woman's lower leg and ankle.]

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:25.140
[Miss Mary:] The lady's ankle is all swelled up; that's another bad sign. 

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:29.050
In the clinic, they keeps checking on three things: 

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:33.950
the patient's weight, her blood pressure, and her urine. 

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:39.140
This lady's clinic chart shows that she had been putting on too much weight, 

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:44.360
especially in the last two months.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:50.970
Her blood pressure had been going up likewise, way above what it ought to be. 

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:58.510
When they tested her urine, it showed up cloudy, full of [inaudible] the doctor said.

00:13:58.510 --> 00:14:02.690
Instead of water clear like a well mother's. 

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:06.180
After Dr. Newton got through explaining all of that,

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:10.490
then the lady agreed herself it was better to let the doctor wait on her. 

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:15.640
Now the nurse is always advising the patient on what to eat and how to take care of themselves.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:24.980
[Miss Penny is speaking to Maybell and pointing out healthful foods, such as an egg, displayed on a table next to them.]

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:31.610
[Miss Mary:] Miss Penny, she keeps a sharp eye out for the puny patients like Maybell,

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:39.140
and if they eat what she say to eat, they mostly gets along okay.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:44.490
[Chorus singing.]

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:49.940
[Maybell's husband plows and she is shown chopping wood in the yard of a home in poor condition.]

00:14:49.940 --> 00:15:02.860
[Miss Mary:] [Now I just didn't know how Maybell was living out there, 11 miles down that [hard-up?] road.

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:16.820
[Maybell walks slowly toward the house and enters the kitchen where a pan of food is on the stove.]

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:20.590
[Miss Mary:] Looked like Maybell done forgot what Miss Penny told her to eat,

00:15:20.590 --> 00:15:26.920
but you know it's hard to eat when you ain't hungry and by yourself all day long.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:36.880
[Maybell walks through the interior of the house, which is sparsely furnished, with walls insulated with tacked-up paper. She checks her face in the mirror.]

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:48.720
[Chorus singing.]

00:15:48.720 --> 00:16:01.100
[Miss Mary:] That place of hers was a regular mess out there.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:06.350
I give her a box myself to start to collecting up her baby things,

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:11.420
but it look like Maybell ain't thinking about nothing such as that.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:21.620
Still it's hard to know just what a person got on his mind sometime.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:33.690
But taking a look at all the mothers that come to the clinic, them that have the trouble is very few.

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:40.180
[It is dark out, and Miss Mary walks up to Ida's house with Ida's husband, Tom.]

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:49.630
[Miss Mary:] Don't worry about that, Tom. Look like all my babies comes at night.

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:53.310
[Aunt Mattie:] Sure been looking out for you, Miss Mary.

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:56.550
[Miss Mary:] Took me a time to wake up, honey.

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:59.490
You said it coming pretty strong, Ida? 

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:03.520
Well, we'll be getting ready right quick.

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:14.030
[Two toddlers are shown asleep in bed. Tom pulls the covers up around their shoulders.]

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:30.030
[Miss Mary:] I need a little more water to rinse off my hands, Aunt Mattie. That'll do fine.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:37.420
Let me see now. Bed made fresh, linens for the bed's ready. 

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:43.190
I wish to goodness all my mothers could have everything fixed up this nice.

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:46.960
I'll have to move the bed over to get under that light.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:54.060
Baby tray fixed. Gonna move that table down this way to lay out my things on.

00:17:54.060 --> 00:18:00.050
Even got the slop jar fixed on the paper. 

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:02.520
Let's see how you're doing, Ida.

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:06.600
[Miss Mary approaches Ida, who sits in a highback chair.]

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:17.930
[Miss Mary:] You're fine, there ain't no hurry.

00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:40.530
[Miss Mary continues to check her sterilized instruments and make her preparations.]

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:49.090
[Ida grimaces.]

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:51.290
[Miss Mary:] I'm watching the clock, honey. 

00:18:51.290 --> 00:19:01.710
[Humming]

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:06.620
You can walk around some if you want to.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:10.610
[Humming]

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:15.540
I remember, Ida, when I was having my third baby. 

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:16.890
[Laughter]

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:26.530
That little old hard-headed boy. He weighed about a...

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:31.660
Just relax yourself and don't think about nothing.

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:32.690
[Ida is in bed now.]

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:40.140
[Miss Mary:] I have known patients to drop right off to sleep between times,

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:54.270
and just sleep and sleep 'til the baby is almost here.

00:19:54.270 --> 00:20:05.470
[Ida's eyes open; Aunt Mattie walks out of the room.]

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:13.290
[Miss Mary cleans her fingernails and scrubs her arms.]

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:21.120
[Scrubbing sound]

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:26.440
[Aunt Mattie thoroughly washes her hands, too.]

00:20:26.440 --> 00:21:11.700
[Mary scrubs and the camera pans over to instruments, jars, and linens at the ready.]

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:20.550
[Miss Mary:] Bear to when you feel one coming, honey,

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:24.700
but pretty soon I want you to start pushing down and pant like a dog.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:26.660
[Panting]

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:29.270
[Laughter]

00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:34.370
[Miss Mary:] Remember now, that's to keep the baby's head from coming down too fast. 

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:38.630
What you want this time, Ida, little girl or a boy?

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:42.330
[Ida:] It don't make no difference to me.

00:21:42.330 --> 00:21:48.550
[Baby crying]

00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:52.880
[Miss Mary:] Warm up the blanket good night, Mattie.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:58.490
He'll be wanting it now as soon as I get the drops in his eyes.

00:21:58.490 --> 00:22:01.000
[Baby crying]

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.900
[Miss Mary:] Hold still now you little scrawny rawny.

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:06.700
You'll soon be through.

00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:10.430
[Ida:] Tell me, Momma, who do he favor?

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:13.760
[Aunt Mattie:] It's too early to tell yet a while, honey.

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:30.010
[Chorus singing.]

00:22:30.010 --> 00:22:45.610
[Miss Mary:] Now, let's see if this youngun knows how to eat.

00:22:45.610 --> 00:22:50.080
You remember what I told you last time, Ida, about nursing your baby right off?

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:54.660
That'll make your womb draw up and you won't lose so much blood. 

00:22:54.660 --> 00:22:56.740
Yes, smart little ole bugger.

00:22:56.740 --> 00:23:05.320
He's catching on to the idea right quick.

00:23:05.320 --> 00:23:17.400
Aunt Mattie, come help me get all my old dirty stuff tied up in my gown.

00:23:17.400 --> 00:23:55.950
[Chorus singing.]

00:23:55.950 --> 00:24:08.220
[Mary returns to her house and sits down on her bed.]

00:24:08.220 --> 00:24:10.550
[Sigh]

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:14.560
[Miss Mary:] Just too wore out to fix a clean bag tonight. 

00:24:14.560 --> 00:24:17.790
I'll fix it early in the morning.

00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:19.140
[Chorus singing.]

00:24:19.140 --> 00:24:21.840
[Mary is dreaming.]

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:26.040
[Doctor in the dream:] What that means, something wasn't clean. 

00:24:26.040 --> 00:24:28.890
Something wasn't clean. 

00:24:28.890 --> 00:24:33.380
Something wasn't clean.

00:24:33.380 --> 00:24:38.880
[Miss Mary:] Lord, just can't sleep with them thoughts preying on my mind.

00:24:38.880 --> 00:24:48.430
[Mary gets out of bed and pulls items from her medical bag.]

00:24:48.430 --> 00:24:51.160
[Maybell's husband Adam runs up and knocks furiously on the door.]

00:24:51.160 --> 00:24:59.590
[Adam:] Miss Mary, Miss Mary, Miss Mary, wake up, Miss Mary. Miss Mary.

00:24:59.590 --> 00:25:05.660
[Miss Mary:] Oh, go away, man. I've just now got into bed.

00:25:05.660 --> 00:25:30.080
[Adam and Mary pull up to Adam and Maybell's house in an old truck and go inside.]

00:25:30.080 --> 00:25:38.830
[Maybell is half on the floor, clutching a chair and crying.]

00:25:38.830 --> 00:25:44.970
[Miss Mary:] Lord, Maybell, what you doing down on that floor?

00:25:44.970 --> 00:25:47.120
[Adam:] Ain't the baby come yet?

00:25:47.120 --> 00:25:51.340
[Miss Mary:] Oh, man, you hush and go bring me some wood here and some water!

00:25:51.340 --> 00:25:58.840
Help with this fire.

00:25:58.840 --> 00:26:04.660
I'm sure glad I brought some newspapers and some clean rags along with me, Maybell.

00:26:04.660 --> 00:26:10.220
Maybell, I just can't deliver no baby on the floor now because it's too dangerous.

00:26:10.220 --> 00:26:12.100
[Maybell:] Yes, Miss Mary.

00:26:12.100 --> 00:26:16.430
[Miss Mary:] You'll find this a heap better anyway. 

00:26:16.430 --> 00:26:18.710
I'ma get my things all boiled up, Maybell,

00:26:18.710 --> 00:26:20.990
and then we'll be ready.

00:26:20.990 --> 00:26:23.460
[Mary boils her instruments over a fire in the fireplace.]

00:26:23.460 --> 00:26:27.760
[Mary scrubs her hands and arms.]

00:26:27.760 --> 00:26:37.630
[Miss Mary:] As ready as I can be with her coming along so fast.

00:26:37.630 --> 00:26:43.060
Make a baby bed out that box; get some use out of it anyway.

00:26:43.060 --> 00:26:50.010
Adam Dudley, come here quick! I need you! 

00:26:50.010 --> 00:26:55.310
I want you to go to the clinic and get me an incubator. Quick!

00:26:55.310 --> 00:26:57.590
[Adam:] This one come dead too, Miss Mary?

00:26:57.590 --> 00:27:00.610
[Miss Mary:] Dead? What do you think? 

00:27:00.610 --> 00:27:02.960
[Mary shows Adam his newborn baby.]

00:27:02.960 --> 00:27:08.950
[Miss Mary:] Hurry now!

00:27:08.950 --> 00:27:31.890
[Mary hums as she goes about her work. The new baby is in a makeshift bassinette with a hot water bottle under the covers and Maybell is in bed.]

00:27:31.890 --> 00:27:39.920
[Miss Mary:] Maybell, now the most important thing for you to do is to keep the baby warm.

00:27:39.920 --> 00:27:45.890
Don't handle him anymore than you just obliged to.

00:27:45.890 --> 00:27:46.870
[Adam arrives at the clinic.]

00:27:46.870 --> 00:27:55.780
[Adam:] Miss Penny, baby come too soon.

00:27:55.780 --> 00:27:59.050
[Miss Mary:] Oh, Miss Penny, I'm glad you come. 

00:27:59.050 --> 00:28:00.430
[Miss Penny and Adam move an incubator into the house.]

00:28:00.430 --> 00:28:02.920
[Miss Penny:] Let's put it at the foot of the bed, Adam, where it's out of the draft.

00:28:02.920 --> 00:28:04.290
[Adam:] Yes, ma'am.

00:28:04.290 --> 00:28:12.960
[Moving sounds]

00:28:12.960 --> 00:28:18.390
[Miss Penny:] You've got to keep this full of hot water all the time to keep this baby warm.

00:28:18.390 --> 00:28:35.570
[Adam:] Yes, ma'am. Then I better go cut some more wood.

00:28:35.570 --> 00:28:38.750
[Unidentified female:] Now I'm goin' and fix Maybell something to eat.

00:28:38.750 --> 00:28:46.420
[Miss Penny:] That's a good idea.

00:28:46.420 --> 00:28:55.650
My, what a husky little peanut we have here. 

00:28:55.650 --> 00:28:59.320
There's nothing wrong with coffee and grits,

00:28:59.320 --> 00:29:04.030
but a mother should have milk and vegetables and meat from the first day on

00:29:04.030 --> 00:29:06.870
to be strong enough to take care of her little baby.

00:29:06.870 --> 00:29:12.210
[Female:] I'll take care of him, Miss Penny. And see that she gets something.

00:29:12.210 --> 00:29:21.260
[Chorus singing.]

00:29:21.260 --> 00:29:26.360
[Miss Mary:] Daddy Adam, come on over here and put your name on your baby's birth certificate.

00:29:26.360 --> 00:29:28.450
What you goin' call him, Adam Junior?

00:29:28.450 --> 00:29:29.730
[Adam:] I reckon.

00:29:29.730 --> 00:29:40.650
[Chorus singing.]

00:29:40.650 --> 00:29:47.770
[Baby is shown with eyes closed, then stretching,]

00:29:52.920 --> 00:29:57.530
[Maybell:] That baby's too little to live, ain't he?

00:29:57.530 --> 00:29:59.440
[Adam:] Oh, Lord, honey.

00:29:59.440 --> 00:30:04.030
[Maybell is crying.]

00:30:04.030 --> 00:30:11.330
[Chorus singing.]

00:30:11.330 --> 00:30:16.290
[Ida is lying in her bed smiling, with her toddler daughter next to her.]

00:30:16.290 --> 00:30:22.850
[Miss Mary:] Next morning I go to see how Ida and her baby gettin' along.

00:30:22.850 --> 00:30:29.090
Looks like everything is fine with Ida and, Lord, that baby. 

00:30:29.090 --> 00:30:35.200
A healthy little ole thing as you ever saw. Yes, he is. 

00:30:35.200 --> 00:30:39.830
Miss Penny come to see about Ida and her new baby, too.

00:30:39.830 --> 00:30:44.630
Aunt Mattie's kinda got old-fashioned ideas. 

00:30:44.630 --> 00:30:48.510
Thinks mommas can't eat things like meat and greens.

00:30:48.510 --> 00:30:55.610
Miss Penny said mommas can eat anything after the babies come that didn't hurt them before the baby come,

00:30:55.610 --> 00:31:00.020
and they feel better for it, too. 

00:31:00.020 --> 00:31:04.840
Baby's cord doin' okay.

00:31:04.840 --> 00:31:10.970
Most of my patients have learned by now, you don't put on anything but a sterile dressing. 

00:31:10.970 --> 00:31:18.680
No grease, no powder.

00:31:18.680 --> 00:31:24.420
[Aunt Mattie delivers a plate of food to Ida.]

00:31:24.420 --> 00:31:36.280
[Chorus singing.]

00:31:36.280 --> 00:31:59.550
[Miss Penny and Miss Mary go about their work; Ida and her daughter eat.]

00:31:59.550 --> 00:32:02.680
[Women are shown in a waiting area, one holding her infant.]

00:32:02.680 --> 00:32:07.470
[Miss Mary:] When Ida come for her six weeks' check-up, Maybell was there, too.

00:32:07.470 --> 00:32:11.180
Poor girl, I felt right sorry for her. 

00:32:11.180 --> 00:32:20.070
Ida just kept bragging about that youngun and all the time Maybell just kept looking and thinking about hers.

00:32:20.070 --> 00:32:37.650
Dr. Newton always checks our mothers to make sure that they didn't have no tears and that their wombs is all right.

00:32:37.650 --> 00:32:43.540
The doctor said Maybell's coming along just fine and look like she's been eating better, too.

00:32:43.540 --> 00:32:48.480
Still Dr. Newton knowed something else had been troubling Maybell this time,

00:32:48.480 --> 00:32:52.870
but Lord, that girl had no call to fret herself. 

00:32:52.870 --> 00:32:57.410
'Cause in four months' time her Adam Junior

00:32:57.410 --> 00:33:02.320
had growed out to be as pretty a baby as you ever saw.

00:33:02.320 --> 00:33:07.730
[A healthy baby Adam is shown, and Maybell looks down at him, smiling.]

00:33:07.730 --> 00:33:12.540
[Chorus singing.]

00:33:12.540 --> 00:33:30.160
[Father Adam is having a photograph taken of himself and baby Adam.]

00:33:30.160 --> 00:33:32.660
[Laughter]

00:33:32.660 --> 00:33:37.720
[Miss Mary:] Well, I'm going to hang my picture of Maybell's baby right up here on the top.

00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:41.580
[Ida:] I bet you're proud of that bitty baby, Miss Mary.

00:33:41.580 --> 00:33:46.530
[Miss Mary:] Why, Ida, I'm proud of all my babies.

00:33:46.530 --> 00:33:54.610
[Chorus singing.]

